
                 Command line editing features of Zeus BBS
                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

   Zeus  allows  you to edit text entered at standard menu prompts with the
following keys.

Back Space         - Delete character to the left of the cursor.
Ctrl-K             - Delete all data entered.
Delete Key         - Delete the character under the cursor.
Cursor Left        - Move the cursor left.
Cursor Right       - Move the cursor right.
Shift Cursor Left  - Position cursor at beginning of line.
Shift Cursor Right - Position cursor at end of line.
Ctrl-O             - Position cursor at the beginning of previous word.
Ctrl-P             - Position cursor at the beginning of next word.

Command Line History

Cursor Up          - Bring up previously entered line in history list
Cursor Down        - Bring up next entered line in history list
Shift Cursor Down  - Sets history pointer to end of list
Shift Cursor Up    - Searches for history lines starting with chars on the
                     left of the cursor on the current line.

   These  keys  now  work with both ANSI and non-ANSI settings and use more
optimised codes...

